WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:06.100
Hidden in Turning Red's story about the messiness
of growing up are a ton of secrets that predict

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.280
the movie's big twists and that Godzilla-sized
finale!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.510
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
in this video I'm explaining all the secret

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.950
symbolism, details and clues in Pixar's latest
hit.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.690
Spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:25.410
There are lots of signs early on in the movie
that, by the end, Mei will choose to embrace

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:26.950
her Red Panda spirit.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:31.990
For example, when she transforms for the first
time, she tries to hide the change she's undergoing

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.850
by wearing a hat to cover up her new red hair.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.520
But there are literally signs everywhere telling
her to be true to herself.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.250
It says "Be Yourself" on the noticeboard right
behind her friends.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.730
And the other words on the board like "loyal",
"caring", and "fun" neatly describe Mei's

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.250
ride-or-die mates and how they'll later support
her when they discover her secret.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:53.469
We love you Mei.

00:00:53.469 --> 00:00:54.829
You're our girl
Yeah.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:56.040
No matter what.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.040
Panda or no panda.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:02.070
There's also the "Dare to be Different, Dare
to be You" poster, an encouragement that she

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:06.170
doesn't need to repress this strange, new
panda version of herself.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.409
Then there's the sign "Nothing Changes if
Nothing Changes", which hints at Mei upending

00:01:11.409 --> 00:01:15.299
her family's tradition of locking away their
panda spirits.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:16.970
And finally, the "Dream BIG!"

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:22.389
poster also anticipates how, in the end, Mei
will decide to keep her furry 8-foot-tall

00:01:22.389 --> 00:01:24.259
side in her life.

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:29.429
When Mei and her squad perform a spontaneous
version of 4*Town's "Nobody Like U" in the

00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:34.490
street, there's another hidden message, this
time, to "Awaken Your Potential Dreams".

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:39.119
On top of that, the 4*Town flyer that Abby
shows Mei reveals that the name of the band's

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:41.039
tour is "BREAKING FREE!".

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:45.359
It's only on screen for a split second, but
it's another subtle suggestion that Meilin

00:01:45.359 --> 00:01:48.999
is going to cut the apron strings and become
her own person.

00:01:48.999 --> 00:01:54.009
And when she high-fives red panda statue Bart
and rubs Lisa's tummy, it's a signal to how

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:58.229
she'll end up accepting both sides of her
identity.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:03.009
Even before we learn the truth about Ming's
own Red Panda transformation as a young woman,

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:07.989
there's plenty of clever clues that ready
us for that reveal and set up the big finale

00:02:07.989 --> 00:02:14.340
with Mei's mum taking on her humongous panda
form once more and their ancestor Sun Yee

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.100
welcoming Red Panda Mei into the world.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:23.220
To begin with notice how both Ming and Sun
Yee one-by-one appear in the shot as Mei tells

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.220
us...

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.240
some of my moves are...
also hers.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:31.980
Which emphasises the crucial panda connection
between all three women.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:37.420
Ming is also framed by two wooden carvings
of red pandas and in the altar picture of

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.800
Sun Yee, there are two more pandas, which
emerge during Mei's nightmare, all of which

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:48.070
points to both the mother and daughter pandas
in the finale and also Sun Yee and Mei's appearance

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:50.620
as red pandas right at the end.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.630
Notice also how, when they exit the temple,
not only is Ming standing next to the much

00:02:55.630 --> 00:03:00.760
angrier looking statue of the two, a hint
to the Mingzilla version of herself, but if

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.910
you look carefully, you'll see that the statue
on the left also has a young red panda under

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:10.090
one of its paws, foreshadowing the dual mother-daughter
transformation.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:16.180
An indication as to just how dangerous Ming's
panda would become was in the scar on Meilin's

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:17.740
grandma's face...

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:22.430
She and your grandma had a terrible fight.
...and you can still spot that scar on Grandma's

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.440
face when she turns into a panda herself.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:30.850
Likewise, Red Panda Ming has a similar hairstyle
to her human counterpart.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.740
And the fact that there are going to be even
more red pandas in the form of her aunties

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.680
and grandma is also signaled during Mei's
nightmare when she sees masses of them run

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.630
over the roof of the family temple.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:47.390
By the way, you can literally see red panda
faces hidden in various accessories worn by

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.670
Mei's aunties, just as you can in Ming's pendant.

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:56.590
Another clue to the final showdown between
Mingzilla and MeiMei is via the welcome mural

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:59.050
that Meilin runs past at the start of the
film.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.900
The wall painting is, of course, in keeping
with the Chinatown location, however each

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.950
creature also represents one of the two women.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:12.270
The green one symbolizes Ming who's predominantly
dressed in green throughout the movie versus

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:16.430
the orangey-red one which represents Mei and
her generally red clothing.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:21.560
And, much of Turning Red is full of clever
colour symbolism that accentuates the differences

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.330
between Mei and her mum.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.060
Red and green are colours that contrast sharply
with one another, so shades of red are often

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:34.560
used around Mei and green for Ming, right
down to their nail varnish, eye shadow, and

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.349
soles of their shoes.

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:41.779
The colour differences emphasise the fact
that Meilin isn't just Ming's mini-me, she's

00:04:41.779 --> 00:04:47.360
her own, distinct person, and Mei coming into
her own as a young adult is the movie's main

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.490
theme.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.110
Some people are like,
"Be careful.

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:55.180
Honoring your parents sounds great, but if
you take it too far, well, you might forget

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.350
to honor yourself."

00:04:56.350 --> 00:05:01.439
Intriguingly, though, both mother and daughter
also have a just splash of the other's colour

00:05:01.439 --> 00:05:05.270
in their outfits:
Mei has a green hair clip and Ming has a red

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.990
pendant, which signals that despite their
differences they're still connected, and it's

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:14.449
also a clue to the fact they both have red
panda spirits.

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:18.960
Another curious detail is that although Ming
dislikes Miriam because she views her as a

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.590
threat to her own relationship with Mei,
Miriam...

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.870
I mean, she's a nice girl, but maybe she's
slowing you down.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:28.529
both Ming and Miriam mostly wear green.

00:05:28.529 --> 00:05:33.430
A hint perhaps that, while they're different
in many ways, Mei's mum and friend have more

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.500
in common than Ming would like to think as,
after all, they both love Mei and, ultimately,

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.080
want the best for her.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:45.330
Mei's grandma and aunties also favour green,
emphasising both their family connection and

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:50.449
the similarity between Ming and her own mother,
whose relationship is also complicated by

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:55.630
feelings of perfectionism and not being good
enough, something we also see happening between

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.569
Mei and Ming.

00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:02.729
Mirroring and symmetry is another technique
used to highlight the state of Mei and Ming's

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:03.729
relationship.

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:08.770
We see this first in the opening family snapshots,
but also in the first scene set at the family

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:09.770
temple.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:10.770
You ready?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.770
Let's do this!

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:17.080
Mei and Ming even sweep in sync with one another,
clean the red panda statues in sync and, after

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.999
a long day, sigh and get up in sync.

00:06:19.999 --> 00:06:25.150
Interestingly, Ming cleans the statue with
the more controlled, calm expression, while

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:30.140
Mei's statue has more of an animated or startled
look, reflecting some of the feelings and

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.749
struggle she'll go through as she transforms.

00:06:32.749 --> 00:06:37.800
After falling out of sync for much of the
film as Mei grows into her own, the mother-daughter

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:43.569
symmetry and mirroring is back again by the
end, after Mei helps Ming deal with her own

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:46.590
issues of inadequacy in relation to Grandma.

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:51.930
Now, if you'd like to discover even more details
hidden in Turning Red such as all the Pixar

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:57.280
references to movies like Luca, Inside Out,
Coco, Lightyear, and Toy Story, tap here to

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.569
watch my Turning Red easter eggs video.

00:06:59.569 --> 00:07:01.860
There's also a link in the video description.

